<!--
  Hand-trimmed fixture standing in for WindowsClient-11-2.7, the latest revision PowerStig ships
  of the Windows 11 STIG. Rule ids, field values and dscresourcemodule attributes are copied from
  the real processed data in the local PowerStig clone rather than invented, so this doubles as
  the field-shape survey #99's map (#98) asked for: every one of the twelve rule types
  WindowsClient-11 carries gets a real rule here, trimmed the way the WindowsServer-2022-DC/-MS
  and WindowsServer-2025-DC/-MS fixtures are (short Description, no VulnDiscussion/RawString
  prose).

  V-253289 (Service) and V-253479 (UserRight) are the same two shapes the WindowsClient-10
  fixture exercises - #100 and #101 fixed both generators against this product's real data too.

  V-253260.a/.b mirrors WindowsClient-10's registry sub-rule pair (same Key, same two values,
  neither half an organisation value). V-253277's real dscresource attribute is WindowsFeature,
  unlike WindowsClient-10's WindowsOptionalFeature - the two products disagree on this attribute
  and dispatch cares about neither, since it keys on the rule-type element.
-->
